openvino_bevfusion: give the BEV-pool scatter a zeroed accumulator.

BEVPoolScatter's GPU kernel only atomic_adds into its int32 output, and
nothing cleared it, so the pooled camera BEV was only right on memory that
happened to be zero. With OpenVINO 2026.3 the first inference was right and
every later one added onto the previous frames. With OpenVINO 2026.5 the GPU
plugin gives the scatter output a reused pool buffer that still holds the
depth logits, so every frame came out as garbage (|BEV| ~2.6e5 instead of
~140) and fusion detected nothing (the detection head's outputs were NaN).

bev_pool.xml now takes the accumulator as a fourth input, bev_accumulator,
that the caller binds once, zeroed. BEVPoolScatter adds into it and returns a
one-element token that orders BEVPoolConvert after it; BEVPoolConvert reads
the accumulator and resets it to zero for the next inference. A model input
is never handed a pool buffer, so this holds whatever the plugin reuses. The
3-input forms of both ops still validate, for IRs exported earlier.

Remove this patch once openvino_contrib carries an equivalent fix.

